WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.899
First we had the Witcher book series, and
then we had the games.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.340
Now we have a promising Netflix series with
a Game of Thrones feel.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:12.160
You don't have to be a super-fan to get on
the Witcher hype train, because this is the

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.419
best time to climb aboard.

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:19.550
The Witcher is, of course, the story of a
witcher, Geralt of Rivia, but the story is

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.580
also about Yennefer and Ciri.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:26.840
Destiny has bound Geralt to these two women,
and it seems the series is going to explore

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:30.400
these ties just as the video games - and,
of course, the books - do.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.760
Henry Cavill, DC's very own Superman, has
taken on the role of Geralt and brought along

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:39.700
his most smoldering, soul-piercing looks and
his stubbly square jaw.

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:44.340
Our two leading ladies, stepping into the
roles of the sorceress Yennefer and the so-called

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.380
"witcher girl" Ciri, are both relatively new
to the acting business.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:54.060
Yennefer is played by Anya Chalotra, whose
eyes are the precise shade of violet as described

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:54.820
in the books.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.320
We don't have smell-o-vision, but we imagine
that she does indeed smell of lilac and gooseberries,

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:00.840
her signature scent.

00:01:01.080 --> 00:01:02.060
"Looking for a woman."

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.620
"Ahhh, like everyone."

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.740
"Not like everyone, and not just every woman.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:10.280
Mine smells of lilac and gooseberries."

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.700
The first glimpse of Geralt's daughter Ciri,
played by Freya Allan, has her looking appropriately

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.440
elfish in a green cloak that serves to bring
out her verdant eyes.

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.020
These first brief glimpses have reassured
fans of the show's attention to detail in

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.240
recreating the books.

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.460
"This child will be extraordinary."

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:32.560
Netflix isn't always forthcoming with release
dates.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.640
They have the benefit of a guaranteed delivery
system: one day the whole series pops up on

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:38.900
one's feed to enjoy.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:40.620
When do we get to enjoy The Witcher?

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.760
Definitely sooner rather than later.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:47.880
We don't have an exact date, but more and
more teasers and information have been paving

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:51.200
the way for the show's eventual release later
in 2019.

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.720
Stranger Things was the hit of summer, so
perhaps the streaming giant is positioning

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.020
The Witcher to be the hit of the fall.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:02.340
The show is expected to be appropriately spooky
for Halloween viewing pleasure.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.660
After all, Geralt's main duty is battling
the ghastly monsters that go bump in the night.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.680
You thought the spider in the swamp at the
end of the trailer was scary?

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.980
Just wait until he encounters a striga or
a wraith later this year.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.860
Netflix pretty much has the power to do anything
it wants, budget-wise.

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:24.140
With everyone and their grandmother subscribed
to the streaming platform, their original

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:28.239
shows are apparently given fairly hefty budgets
when it comes to production.

00:02:28.239 --> 00:02:32.680
The Witcher will consist of eight episodes
- that's eight hours of fantasy magic and

00:02:32.680 --> 00:02:37.710
mayhem - and the producers have promised that
each and every episode will be, quote, "epic

00:02:37.710 --> 00:02:38.200
in scale."

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:42.720
Showrunner Lauren Hissrich assured Witcher
fans via Twitter that the show wasn't going

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:43.380
to look cheap.

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:44.080
She wrote:

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:45.760
"TV budgets are big.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:46.620
They are.

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:51.020
We'll be using money as wisely as we can,
to do as much as we can.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.420
(Monsters included - and still very much in
hot discussion)."

00:02:54.760 --> 00:02:59.379
Hissrich also mentioned that she wasn't going
to try to pack in too much plot in these eight

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:03.659
episodes, so as to allow for relationships
and characters to grow naturally.

00:03:03.880 --> 00:03:05.000
You know what that means?

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.260
More seasons.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:11.319
While we don't have any concrete numbers regarding
The Witcher's budget, Netflix seems to have

00:03:11.319 --> 00:03:16.170
granted the show enough cash for to lay the
foundation for a pretty special experience.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.220
There are eight books in The Witcher series.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.300
We highly doubt that each episode will try
to cram an entire novel into an hour, so we're

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.240
left to wonder which stories have been chosen
for this season on Netflix.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:33.040
The books take their time, allowing readers
to get to know Geralt and his world of monsters.

00:03:33.390 --> 00:03:37.820
Taking a look at the named characters in the
cast, some of the plot seems to have been

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.680
pulled from the prequel book, The Last Wish.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:45.180
On the other hand, the trailer shows scenes
ripped straight from the following book, Blood

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:45.940
of Elves.

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:51.890
In the first volume of Geralt's story, this
installment finds him raising Ciri in Kaer

00:03:51.890 --> 00:03:56.680
Morhen, but eventually takes her out and into
the world at the sorceress Triss' prodding.

00:03:56.720 --> 00:04:02.060
This is where Yennefer comes in, and Ciri
exchanges her witcher training — all sword

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:05.180
fighting and pirouettes — for a focus on
magic.

00:04:06.109 --> 00:04:10.180
No matter the narrative path that Hissrich
and company take in telling the fantastical

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:15.579
tale of Geralt, Yennefer, and Ciri, one thing
is for certain — it will be a road paved

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.640
with twists, turns, and intrigue….

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.260
And stained in a heaping helping of blood.

00:04:20.920 --> 00:04:25.940
Andrzej Sapkowski, the author behind Geralt,
isn't a big fan of the various adaptations

00:04:25.940 --> 00:04:26.800
of his books.

00:04:27.340 --> 00:04:29.020
He's not bitter — just busy.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:33.840
He has said that he never played the games
based on his books, not because he didn't

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.200
like them, but because he's a writer and he's
got writing to do.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:38.880
He is, after all, a professional.

00:04:39.480 --> 00:04:42.080
“This world doesn't need a hero…

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.660
It needs a professional."

00:04:47.140 --> 00:04:51.880
Apparently, he has applied this same attitude
to the Netflix adaptation and has been utterly

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.600
hands-off with the production.

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.760
Sapkowski told Portugese website JPN:

00:04:57.000 --> 00:05:03.100
"In all adaptations, be it the first or the
last, I am never involved in its development.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.180
From my point of view, the book is the book
and adaptation is adaptation."

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.880
Showrunner Lauren Hissrich has assured fans
that the Netflix adaptation has the author's

00:05:11.880 --> 00:05:13.580
seal of approval, however.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.100
Perhaps in an effort to prove that she really
knows her stuff, Hissrich's Twitter has been

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:22.940
a veritable treasure trove of maybe-spoilers,
cryptically answering fans' questions with

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:26.700
winks and nudges as to what our first season
with Geralt will entail.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:31.400
She has continually referred back to the books
as the solid basis on which The Witcher's

00:05:31.400 --> 00:05:33.460
Netflix adaptation has been written.

